From: User <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] SysV IPC and POSIX message queues fail with ENOSYS

shm*, sem*, msg* and mq_* return their error value with errno ENOSYS and
issue no syscall (shmat returns (void *) -1; mq_notify fails before its
SIGEV_THREAD set-up): the answer of a kernel built without CONFIG_SYSVIPC
and CONFIG_POSIX_MQUEUE. Only the 64-bit-time paths aarch64 uses change.

No SysV IPC or mq_* syscall is in the Android 13 (API 33) app seccomp
allowlist; the filter traps them with SIGSYS.
---
--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/shmget.c
+++ b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/shmget.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <sys/msg.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <ipc_priv.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 #include <sysdep.h>
 
 /* Return an identifier for an shared memory segment of at least size SIZE
@@ -26,9 +27,7 @@
 int
 shmget (key_t key, size_t size, int shmflg)
 {
-#ifdef __ASSUME_DIRECT_SYSVIPC_SYSCALLS
-  return INLINE_SYSCALL_CALL (shmget, key, size, shmflg, NULL);
-#else
-  return INLINE_SYSCALL_CALL (ipc, IPCOP_shmget, key, size, shmflg, NULL);
-#endif
+  /* SysV IPC syscalls are trapped by the Android app seccomp policy:
+     fail without issuing one.  */
+  return INLINE_SYSCALL_ERROR_RETURN_VALUE (ENOSYS);
 }
